WEBVTT

00:01.040 --> 00:03.440
[Thomas]
My name is Thomas Shelby,

00:03.520 --> 00:05.600
and today, I'm going to kill a man.

00:07.920 --> 00:09.680
Today is Derby Day,

00:10.280 --> 00:14.280
and the murder will take place
this afternoon at the Epsom races...

00:22.120 --> 00:25.680
It may be that I'm able
to escape after the killing.

00:25.760 --> 00:27.400
The odds are not good,

00:27.480 --> 00:30.040
which is why
I'm writing this letter...

00:30.120 --> 00:33.320
I've been forced by agents
of the crown to carry out this murder,

00:33.400 --> 00:38.240
and in the event of my own death
I want the following facts to be known:

00:38.320 --> 00:40.920
My family are innocent
of any involvement.

00:46.200 --> 00:48.000
Who are we?

00:48.080 --> 00:51.280
- [all] Small Heath Rifles!
- [John] Let's go!

00:51.360 --> 00:53.720
[men shouting]

01:00.040 --> 01:02.280
[Thomas] And while some of them
maybe guilty of other things...

01:04.599 --> 01:07.360
...I've not shared details
of this mission with any of them

01:07.440 --> 01:10.200
and how company assets
were used...

01:15.720 --> 01:17.640
Agents of the Crown joined forces

01:17.720 --> 01:20.480
with pro-treaty Fenians
to arrange this murder.

01:20.560 --> 01:24.120
I believe the government intend
to falsely blame the anti-treaty IRA.

01:24.200 --> 01:26.560
Therefore,
the bullet I fire this afternoon

01:26.680 --> 01:29.160
will be the starting gun
for civil war in Ireland.

01:29.240 --> 01:31.440
- [bed creaking rhythmically]
- [panting]

01:31.520 --> 01:34.560
The man I've been instructed to kill
is Field Marshal Russell,

01:34.640 --> 01:36.880
formerly a Black and Tan commander

01:36.960 --> 01:40.000
who committed many atrocities
in the county of Cork.

01:40.080 --> 01:43.640
There's no remorse in my heart
at the prospect of his death.

01:43.720 --> 01:47.280
However, the conspiracy behind the killing
is cause for international concern.

01:47.360 --> 01:49.560
Such is the gravity of my secret mission

01:49.640 --> 01:52.880
that after I've served my purpose
I believe they intend to kill me.

01:52.960 --> 01:53.920
Do you want tea?

01:54.000 --> 01:58.400
[Thomas] I therefore want to name
a particular individual in this letter...

01:58.760 --> 02:01.840
The agent who's initiated
and orchestrated this crime

02:01.920 --> 02:03.760
is Major Chester Campbell

02:03.840 --> 02:06.320
of the British
Secret Intelligence Service.

02:07.320 --> 02:10.759
He chose me for this dirty business
as an act of vengeance,

02:10.840 --> 02:12.880
prompted by hatred
of longstanding.

02:13.720 --> 02:15.360
In the event of my death

02:15.440 --> 02:18.320
it is imperative he be
brought to justice.

02:18.400 --> 02:21.400
If you're reading this,
then I'm dead already.

02:21.480 --> 02:24.640
I hope that living as you do,
in a truly free country,

02:24.720 --> 02:28.080
you'll be able to make the above facts
known to the world.

02:28.160 --> 02:30.920
Yours sincerely, Thomas Shelby.

02:32.440 --> 02:34.840
Did you in anyway, you ignorant git.

02:34.920 --> 02:36.000
Ada.

02:36.080 --> 02:37.600
Sit down here for a minute.

02:41.560 --> 02:44.680
Ada, if anything happens to me today...

02:49.080 --> 02:50.920
...I need you to post this letter.

02:52.560 --> 02:53.960
Stamp's already on.

02:54.040 --> 02:58.160
Don't ask any questions,
it's... to do with insurance.

03:02.040 --> 03:04.120
Look, Tommy?

03:05.000 --> 03:08.640
Whatever it is you're involved in,
just tell us.

03:11.120 --> 03:12.920
God, you never let anybody in.

03:16.080 --> 03:17.520
We love you, Tom.

03:20.800 --> 03:23.800
What are you doing
up at six o'clock in the morning?

03:25.200 --> 03:27.880
- Ready?
- [Ada] What the bloody hell is going on?

03:27.960 --> 03:29.200
Little errand.

03:29.280 --> 03:30.840
What errand?

03:30.920 --> 03:33.760
- He just has to stand there, Ada.
- Stand where?

03:33.840 --> 03:36.520
- Let's go, come on.
- James, what's going on?

03:36.600 --> 03:39.560
Don't listen to him, James.
He'll get you killed.

03:39.640 --> 03:41.440
What errand?

03:41.520 --> 03:43.040
For the cause, Ada.

03:44.040 --> 03:45.480
The good old cause.

03:59.400 --> 04:01.440
[footsteps approaching]

04:01.520 --> 04:04.400
[song playing]

04:06.400 --> 04:07.720
[door unlocks]

04:11.880 --> 04:13.560
Hands off cocks, on with socks.

04:13.640 --> 04:15.560
One at a time...

04:15.640 --> 04:17.480
One at a time,
that's all I ask.

04:18.680 --> 04:21.320
You're getting out, Mr. Shelby.

04:22.320 --> 04:23.680
[sighs]

04:35.400 --> 04:38.680
All ten witnesses against you
withdrew their statements.

04:39.080 --> 04:40.240
Last night.

04:41.560 --> 04:42.560
All at once.

04:42.640 --> 04:43.880
At nine o'clock.

04:44.840 --> 04:47.080
Don't ask me why,
because I don't know.

04:48.920 --> 04:52.400
For the next ten minutes
you don't do or say anything

04:52.480 --> 04:53.480
I haven't told you, all right?

04:54.280 --> 04:55.640
- All right?
- Yeah.

04:57.640 --> 04:59.000
Hello, Ollie.

05:00.160 --> 05:01.440
Oi, hang on.

05:01.880 --> 05:03.840
Just you, yeah?
He stays out here.

05:05.600 --> 05:06.640
You stay here.

05:08.280 --> 05:12.240
[song continues]

05:46.440 --> 05:48.240
Johnny fucking Dogs.

05:50.160 --> 05:53.040
[exhales heavily]
How did he get me out of there?

05:53.120 --> 05:56.480
I need to get you to a telephone.
You need to make a call.

05:56.560 --> 05:58.400
It's all part of
Tommy's plan...

05:58.480 --> 06:00.320
- [engine starts]
- ...apparently.

06:08.520 --> 06:11.560
[phone ringing]

06:11.640 --> 06:13.960
That will probably be
for you, won't it?

06:20.320 --> 06:21.520
Hello.

06:22.360 --> 06:23.520
Arthur?

06:24.360 --> 06:25.560
You're out?

06:31.080 --> 06:35.200
Right, so that will be your side
of the street swept up, won't it?

06:37.120 --> 06:38.920
Where is mine?

06:39.000 --> 06:40.520
What have you got for me?

06:46.760 --> 06:49.240
Signed by the Minister
of the Empire himself.

06:49.320 --> 06:51.800
Yes... [mumbles]

06:51.880 --> 06:54.640
Which means that you can put
your rum in our shipments

06:54.720 --> 06:57.320
and no one at Poplar Docks
will lift a canvas.

06:57.400 --> 07:00.280
You know what, I'm not even going to
have my lawyer look at that.

07:00.400 --> 07:03.360
- [Thomas] No, no, it's all legal.
- You know what, mate, I trust you.

07:03.440 --> 07:05.400
That's that. Done.

07:05.480 --> 07:08.880
So, whiskey.
[sighs]

07:08.960 --> 07:13.160
There is one thing though
that we do need to discuss.

07:13.240 --> 07:14.440
What would that be?

07:14.520 --> 07:20.400
It says here 20 percent
paid to me of your export business.

07:21.520 --> 07:24.200
- As we agreed on the telephone.
- No, no, no.

07:24.280 --> 07:27.880
You see, I have had my lawyer
draw this up

07:28.160 --> 07:31.000
for us, just in case...

07:31.080 --> 07:32.800
Hear that.
[clears throat]

07:33.920 --> 07:35.680
It says that...

07:36.440 --> 07:39.080
Right here, that a hundred percent

07:39.160 --> 07:43.080
of your business...
goes to me.

07:46.200 --> 07:48.160
- I see.
- It's there, but...

07:48.240 --> 07:51.560
...don't worry about it, right,
because it is totally legal binding.

07:51.640 --> 07:53.400
All you have to do
is sign the document

07:53.480 --> 07:55.640
and transfer the whole lot over to me.

07:55.720 --> 07:58.080
- Sign just here is it?
- Yeah.

07:58.160 --> 07:59.320
I see.

07:59.400 --> 08:01.360
That's funny, that is.

08:01.920 --> 08:03.040
What?

08:03.120 --> 08:04.520
Now that's funny.

08:05.560 --> 08:08.360
I'll give you 100 percent
of my business?

08:10.760 --> 08:11.760
Yeah.

08:13.400 --> 08:14.720
Why?

08:19.480 --> 08:21.760
Ollie, no. No, no.

08:21.840 --> 08:24.520
Put that down, he understands.
He understands.

08:24.680 --> 08:26.800
He's a big boy, he knows the road.

08:26.880 --> 08:29.520
Now, look,
it's just non-fucking negotiable.

08:29.600 --> 08:30.960
That's all you need to know.

08:31.040 --> 08:34.000
So all you have to do
is sign the fucking contract.

08:34.080 --> 08:35.559
- Right there.
- Just sign it?

08:35.640 --> 08:36.919
With your pen.

08:37.000 --> 08:38.480
- I understand.
- Good.

08:38.840 --> 08:39.880
Get on with it.

08:39.960 --> 08:43.039
Well, I have an associate
waiting for me at the door.

08:44.280 --> 08:46.480
I know that he looks
like a choir boy,

08:46.560 --> 08:50.320
but he's actually an anarchist
from Kentish Town.

08:50.400 --> 08:55.080
Tommy, I'm going
to fucking shoot you. All right?

08:55.240 --> 08:57.760
Now, when I came
in here, Mr. Solomons,

08:57.840 --> 08:59.640
I stopped to tie my shoe lace.

09:00.080 --> 09:02.240
Isn't that a fact, Ollie?

09:02.400 --> 09:04.880
I stopped to tie my shoelace.

09:04.960 --> 09:06.480
And while I was doing it,

09:06.560 --> 09:09.480
I laid a hand grenade
under one of your barrels.

09:09.560 --> 09:12.120
Mark 15 with wire trip.

09:12.200 --> 09:14.600
And my friend upstairs...

09:14.680 --> 09:17.200
Well, he's like one of those
anarchists that, uh,

09:17.280 --> 09:19.160
they blew up Wall Street, you know?

09:19.560 --> 09:21.000
He's a professional.

09:21.080 --> 09:22.960
And he's in charge of the wire.

09:23.520 --> 09:25.600
If I don't walk out of that door

09:25.680 --> 09:27.880
by the stroke of seven,

09:27.960 --> 09:34.040
he's going to trigger the grenade and...
your very combustible rum

09:34.120 --> 09:36.280
will blow us all to hell.

09:39.120 --> 09:40.480
And I don't care.

09:43.240 --> 09:45.120
Because I'm already dead.

09:50.560 --> 09:53.280
He tied his lace, Alfie,
and there is a kid at the door.

09:53.640 --> 09:56.640
From a good family too, Ollie.
It's shocking what they become.

09:56.760 --> 09:58.600
What were you doing
when this happened?

09:58.680 --> 10:01.800
- He tied his lace, nothing else.
- Yeah, well, what were you doing?

10:02.400 --> 10:04.640
I was marking the runners
in the paper.

10:06.440 --> 10:07.760
What are you doing?

10:07.840 --> 10:10.040
Just checking the time.
Carry on...

10:10.560 --> 10:13.280
All right, Ollie, I want you
to go outside, yeah,

10:13.360 --> 10:16.560
and shoot that boy
in the face from the good family.

10:16.640 --> 10:20.320
Anyone walks through that door
except me, he blows the grenade.

10:21.720 --> 10:24.720
- He tied his fucking lace, Alfie.
- I did tie my lace.

10:26.720 --> 10:33.200
I bet, 100-1,
that you're fucking lying, mate.

10:33.280 --> 10:34.640
That's my money.

10:34.760 --> 10:37.160
Well, you've failed to consider the form.

10:37.240 --> 10:41.400
I did blow up my own pub
for the insurance.

10:45.240 --> 10:49.960
[Solomons] OK, well, considering the form,
I would say 65-1.

10:50.040 --> 10:52.840
Very good odds.
And I would be more than happy to agree

10:52.920 --> 10:55.720
for you to sign over 65%
of your business to me.

10:55.800 --> 10:57.440
- Make it--
- Sixty five?

10:57.520 --> 10:59.640
No deal.
Ollie, what do you say?

10:59.720 --> 11:02.880
Jesus Christ, Alfie,
he tied his fucking lace. I saw him.

11:02.960 --> 11:05.760
Look, he planted a grenade,
I know he did.

11:05.840 --> 11:07.720
Alfie, he's Tommy fucking Shelby--

11:07.800 --> 11:10.560
[panting]

11:10.800 --> 11:13.400
You're behaving
like a fucking child.

11:13.480 --> 11:15.040
This is a man's world.

11:16.760 --> 11:20.680
Now take that apron off,
and sit in the corner like a little boy.

11:21.120 --> 11:23.120
Fuck off! Now!

11:27.840 --> 11:29.040
Four minutes.

11:29.120 --> 11:30.600
Right, four minutes.

11:31.120 --> 11:32.960
Talk to me about hand grenades.

11:33.040 --> 11:35.880
The chalk mark on the barrel
at knee height

11:35.960 --> 11:37.720
said "Hamilton, Christmas."

11:37.800 --> 11:40.200
I took out the pin
and put it on the wire.

11:59.000 --> 12:00.400
Based on this...

12:05.200 --> 12:07.480
- ...forty-five percent.
- Thirty.

12:07.560 --> 12:10.320
Oh, fuck off, Tommy,
that's far too little.

12:14.200 --> 12:19.960
In France, Mr. Solomon, when I was
a tunneler, a clay kicker, 1-7-9...

12:21.880 --> 12:23.560
I blew up Schwaben Hohe.

12:25.480 --> 12:27.280
Same kit I'm using today.

12:28.680 --> 12:30.080
That's funny, that.

12:32.520 --> 12:37.440
I do know the 1-7-9,
and I heard they all got buried.

12:38.960 --> 12:40.840
Three of us dug ourselves out.

12:40.920 --> 12:43.000
Are you digging yourself out now?

12:44.440 --> 12:46.240
Like I'm digging now.

12:49.560 --> 12:51.080
[whispering] Fuck me!

12:54.080 --> 12:58.280
Listen, I'll give you 35 percent.
That's your lot.

13:00.640 --> 13:01.840
Thirty-five.

13:23.440 --> 13:25.880
- You're late.
- Please, I had business.

13:27.280 --> 13:28.280
[groans]

13:28.360 --> 13:31.960
- How did you get me out of that?
- I need you today, brother.

13:32.040 --> 13:33.720
We pulled some strings.

13:33.960 --> 13:35.680
- You all right?
- I am now.

13:37.560 --> 13:39.400
So Arthur's back in charge now?

13:39.480 --> 13:40.920
He's in charge of you.

13:41.000 --> 13:44.480
And you're both in charge of him.
Lookout duties only today.

13:44.560 --> 13:45.960
- Tom, I'm getting sick of this--
- Finn,

13:46.040 --> 13:48.320
you don't obey orders,
you don't come.

13:49.680 --> 13:51.280
- Johnny Dogs.
- Tommy.

13:51.360 --> 13:55.160
- Your boys will meet us there?
- Well, the Lees will be there, captain.

13:56.640 --> 13:57.720
Captain?

13:57.800 --> 13:59.120
I've promoted you.

13:59.320 --> 14:02.280
Well, the boys say that you're no longer
like a sergeant major.

14:02.360 --> 14:05.400
Fucking those rich women
and using those fancy words.

14:05.480 --> 14:07.760
I'd say you're more like
a captain these days.

14:07.840 --> 14:10.160
Fine, well, I'll take it as a compliment.

14:10.840 --> 14:12.240
Just don't bloody shoot me.

14:12.320 --> 14:14.200
Let's go to the Derby, boys.

14:14.480 --> 14:17.200
All right, then. Light them up!

14:17.280 --> 14:20.400
[phone ringing]

14:24.320 --> 14:25.440
Hello.

14:26.480 --> 14:28.560
No, I'm afraid Mr. Shelby is in London.

14:29.680 --> 14:31.600
- He can't be reached.
- [door opens]

14:31.680 --> 14:34.320
- No, he won't be back today.
- [door closes]

14:34.400 --> 14:35.680
He's at the races.

14:35.760 --> 14:37.800
The Epsom races, the Epsom Derby.

14:38.600 --> 14:40.040
Can I ask who's calling?

14:47.960 --> 14:49.440
I'm going to the station.

15:18.920 --> 15:20.000
[sighs]

15:21.360 --> 15:22.240
What's that?

15:22.320 --> 15:23.560
That money is yours.

15:28.080 --> 15:29.320
You take the money,

15:30.000 --> 15:34.400
you get a train
and you start a new life in London.

15:35.080 --> 15:37.720
I don't want to see you here
when I get back.

15:41.480 --> 15:42.840
If I get back.

15:45.040 --> 15:47.720
Everything is an "if"
in this Birmingham life.

15:48.360 --> 15:50.960
You can write on Sundays.

15:51.440 --> 15:53.320
And visit on holy days.

15:53.600 --> 15:57.480
But I want you to wash this city
out of your hair and your clothes.

15:58.720 --> 16:01.240
That's what I should have
done at the start.

16:01.320 --> 16:03.360
Now, I've got business to attend to.

16:10.680 --> 16:12.120
I do love you, Michael.

16:14.000 --> 16:15.320
I love you, too.

16:18.520 --> 16:20.040
You'll miss your train.

17:00.040 --> 17:02.360
[Campbell]
My beloved greyhounds.

17:04.800 --> 17:06.000
Behold.

17:08.560 --> 17:09.839
Today's rabbit.

17:13.319 --> 17:14.920
When I give you the signal,

17:15.000 --> 17:17.440
I want you to send that man to his maker.

17:20.240 --> 17:22.200
I've decided to use you men

17:22.280 --> 17:24.839
because I couldn't trust
the hearts and the livers

17:24.920 --> 17:29.080
of the English pansies and posies
they'd given me as operatives.

17:30.000 --> 17:31.680
Now... [clears throat]

17:32.880 --> 17:35.040
This is a man of some capability.

17:37.080 --> 17:41.880
But I expect no excuses
and no failures.

17:41.960 --> 17:44.720
The Red Right Hand
of the Ulster volunteer force

17:44.800 --> 17:46.880
will not let you down,
Mr. Campbell.

17:49.760 --> 17:51.320
The Red Right Hand.

17:53.400 --> 17:55.000
Good luck, gentlemen.

17:55.320 --> 17:58.160
[song playing]

18:11.760 --> 18:14.800
[Thomas] Gentlemen,
today we are not fucking about.

18:14.920 --> 18:16.760
I hope you've all
obeyed instructions

18:16.840 --> 18:18.600
and brought loaded firearms with you.

18:18.680 --> 18:19.720
- Yes.
- Yeah.

18:19.800 --> 18:23.200
Good. You will all know that if you
are lifted on a racetrack these days

18:23.280 --> 18:25.080
with a loaded weapon,
you get 20 years.

18:25.160 --> 18:27.960
That's all right,
today you won't get lifted.

18:28.040 --> 18:30.600
Because, today, there will be
no coppers will be around to lift you.

18:30.680 --> 18:33.200
At exactly three o'clock,
there will be an incident

18:33.280 --> 18:34.720
in the owner's enclosure,

18:34.800 --> 18:37.560
and all the coppers in the track
will be diverted, all of them.

18:37.640 --> 18:39.640
They'll be looking for someone.

18:39.720 --> 18:41.400
You will be free to operate at will.

18:41.480 --> 18:44.360
- Looking for who?
- Me, they will be looking for me.

18:44.440 --> 18:46.000
Now, while the coppers are busy with me,

18:46.080 --> 18:47.560
you will make your move
on Sabini's pitches.

18:47.640 --> 18:51.640
You confiscate his takings, you destroy
his licenses and you do it at gun point.

18:51.720 --> 18:54.320
He usually has police protection
so he won't be armed.

18:54.400 --> 18:58.240
We should aim to complete the takeover
without a shot being fired, understood?

18:58.320 --> 18:59.600
And remember,

18:59.680 --> 19:02.680
the licenses are more important
than the takings.

19:02.760 --> 19:04.800
All right,
before the fun begins,

19:04.880 --> 19:07.600
you can all lay ten bob
on Nom De Guerre.

19:07.680 --> 19:10.360
- I hear she's going to win.
- [all cheer]

19:10.440 --> 19:12.680
Only beer beforehand, boys.

19:12.760 --> 19:15.080
There will be time
for rum and whiskey after.

19:15.480 --> 19:18.440
And remember,
do not make a move until three,

19:18.520 --> 19:20.080
when the coppers leave.

19:20.160 --> 19:22.400
- That is all.
- Really lucky, John.

19:22.480 --> 19:23.720
[Arthur] Incidents...

19:23.800 --> 19:28.240
What are you going to do that every
copper at the Derby look the other way?

19:28.880 --> 19:30.160
Trust me, brother.

19:31.040 --> 19:32.560
[John] Right, over here.

19:32.640 --> 19:34.600
Hey, boys, come here.

19:34.680 --> 19:38.360
- [people chattering]
- [indistinct announcement over PA]

19:55.000 --> 19:56.000
Ten, please.

20:08.920 --> 20:11.160
[announcement over PA
in distance]

20:15.560 --> 20:17.880
She threw a shoe
coming out of the box.

20:21.280 --> 20:22.360
Eh?

20:25.160 --> 20:26.800
She looks in fine shape.

20:27.720 --> 20:29.400
Hello, hello, hello.

20:29.480 --> 20:32.400
[speaking foreign language]

20:37.160 --> 20:38.560
Should I be worried?

20:38.800 --> 20:39.880
You should not.

20:41.200 --> 20:42.880
Go and drink, enjoy the day.

20:42.960 --> 20:44.960
I'll come and find you
when the race is done.

20:46.040 --> 20:49.080
Hmm. That's nice. Is that yours?

20:49.760 --> 20:52.160
My mother wore it
to the Derby in 1895.

20:53.080 --> 20:55.440
She was presented
to Queen Victoria.

20:56.720 --> 20:58.640
After the race,
I'll change in the horse box

20:58.720 --> 21:02.000
and come and join you with the toffs.
What do you say?

21:02.120 --> 21:04.560
Hmm. Yeah.

21:08.080 --> 21:09.640
You don't want me to join you.

21:12.760 --> 21:14.960
It's fine, I'll sit out here
in the mud.

21:27.360 --> 21:29.080
Whatever happens today,

21:30.000 --> 21:31.200
it was good.

21:31.800 --> 21:33.720
[breathes deeply]

21:33.800 --> 21:35.280
You mean, win or lose?

21:37.360 --> 21:39.640
Yeah, win or lose.

21:41.680 --> 21:43.840
You know,
I never watch the race.

21:43.920 --> 21:45.280
Can't stand it.

21:46.080 --> 21:48.840
I always like to find
somewhere dark and quiet.

21:52.560 --> 21:53.600
Tommy?

21:55.520 --> 21:57.320
If you can't find me up there,

21:58.440 --> 22:00.160
I'll come and find you later.

22:01.840 --> 22:02.920
What do you mean?

22:03.320 --> 22:04.800
Whatever happens to me...

22:06.160 --> 22:07.240
...no regrets.

22:08.480 --> 22:09.760
No regrets.

22:11.440 --> 22:12.720
And I will find you.

22:14.840 --> 22:16.000
All right.

22:16.560 --> 22:18.000
Remember that.

22:19.120 --> 22:20.040
Bye.

22:25.960 --> 22:28.160
[people chattering]

22:34.400 --> 22:36.400
Put this on Nom De Guerre.

22:45.920 --> 22:48.520
- [man 1] Good day, sir.
- [man 2] Sabini.

22:51.360 --> 22:52.440
There he is.

22:56.800 --> 22:58.560
Fucking meatball bollocks.

23:00.320 --> 23:01.720
All right, let's go.

23:57.480 --> 23:59.000
I have to talk to you.

23:59.480 --> 24:02.880
- Grace, what are you doing here?
- I have to talk to you.

24:02.960 --> 24:04.040
Grace.

24:05.720 --> 24:07.200
This is not a good time.

24:12.040 --> 24:14.040
Let's go this way.
Excuse us.

24:15.520 --> 24:17.360
Whatever it is, Grace, it'll have to wait.

24:17.440 --> 24:20.040
I can't wait.
It wasn't me who is at fault.

24:21.520 --> 24:22.800
I'm pregnant.

24:24.440 --> 24:26.040
The baby is yours.

24:32.760 --> 24:34.120
But he'll believe?

24:35.000 --> 24:36.840
Make your husband
believe that it's his.

24:36.920 --> 24:38.680
Is that what
you want me to do?

24:38.760 --> 24:41.760
Grace, I seriously
have things to do.

24:41.840 --> 24:43.240
It's not worth the toss
of a coin this time?

24:43.320 --> 24:46.880
Grace, I have things to do.
When they are...

24:46.960 --> 24:50.160
- When they are done, I will decide.
- When will that be?

24:50.240 --> 24:51.640
- After the race.
- After the race?

24:51.720 --> 24:53.560
After the fucking race, Tommy?

24:53.640 --> 24:56.040
When the race is over,
I will decide what to do.

24:56.120 --> 24:57.920
What to fucking do, all right?

24:58.000 --> 24:59.320
But, Tommy...

25:00.120 --> 25:01.920
...I was right not to tell him.

25:02.880 --> 25:05.560
I could have phoned him
and lied but I didn't.

25:05.640 --> 25:09.440
Just tell me that I was right
not to phone and lie.

25:09.880 --> 25:11.720
Agree with that, Tommy.

25:13.280 --> 25:14.440
Yes.

25:15.120 --> 25:16.080
Yes, Grace.

25:16.160 --> 25:17.960
Because the thing is...

25:20.200 --> 25:21.960
...I love you, not him.

25:25.640 --> 25:27.280
That is a thing.

25:32.760 --> 25:35.840
- A baby Thomas.
- Yes.

25:39.640 --> 25:42.480
- Go to your race.
- Where will you be?

25:42.560 --> 25:43.680
I'll be waiting.

25:44.960 --> 25:47.080
I'll wait where they lay the bets.

25:54.280 --> 25:56.160
[music playing]

26:05.960 --> 26:08.040
[people chattering]

26:21.840 --> 26:22.680
[horse neighing]

26:22.760 --> 26:24.200
I found the lost sheep.

26:25.080 --> 26:26.600
Come on, Lizzie.

26:29.040 --> 26:30.960
- What do you think?
- About what?

26:31.400 --> 26:34.200
- About the dress.
- Undo two buttons. Come on!

26:41.000 --> 26:43.560
Oh, Tommy, I never thought
I'd see the like of this.

26:43.640 --> 26:44.800
Yeah.

26:45.880 --> 26:49.000
But I do know that I need to work,
so maybe now's not time to take a drink.

26:49.080 --> 26:53.880
Well, here.
Take this, you might need it.

26:59.280 --> 27:02.320
What work do you want me
to do for you today, Tommy?

27:02.440 --> 27:04.360
To take your notes on a meeting?

27:04.440 --> 27:07.040
No, Lizzie, you're not here
to take notes.

27:07.720 --> 27:09.640
My short hand won't be required?

27:11.000 --> 27:12.280
Lizzie...

27:16.800 --> 27:18.080
There's a man here,

27:18.160 --> 27:21.600
and I need him separated from the crowd
and taken to a quiet place.

27:21.680 --> 27:23.040
A quiet place.

27:23.120 --> 27:26.160
- Lizzie, I know what I said.
- Yeah, you know.

27:26.240 --> 27:29.160
You know, you told me I shouldn't
do that kind of work anymore.

27:29.240 --> 27:31.520
I just need you to isolate him is all.

27:31.600 --> 27:35.600
- "No exceptions", you said.
- I have drawn a map, all right,

27:36.360 --> 27:38.520
of where exactly
you need to take him...

27:38.600 --> 27:42.080
For months, I've made no exceptions
because you told me not to.

27:42.160 --> 27:46.120
Lizzie... just keep him busy
at the place marked with an "x,"

27:46.200 --> 27:49.800
and I'll get to you before it can start,
I promise, all right?

27:51.960 --> 27:54.200
Mustn't smudge my eyes.
He might not like that.

27:54.280 --> 27:57.480
Lizzie, this is the only time.

27:57.560 --> 27:59.800
After this, never again.

28:00.840 --> 28:02.520
I'd like to pay you an extra five--

28:02.600 --> 28:04.600
Do not talk to me
about money now.

28:04.680 --> 28:08.080
Not right now, I swear I'll break
this glass in your eyes.

28:09.720 --> 28:11.160
[Thomas clears his throat]

28:11.240 --> 28:16.000
No exceptions, there's been no hardship.
You know why?

28:18.680 --> 28:19.800
Mm?

28:23.480 --> 28:24.800
Doesn't matter.

28:26.760 --> 28:30.560
- Who is he?
- To your right, soldier.

28:31.600 --> 28:33.080
Smoking a cigarette.

28:33.200 --> 28:35.040
Just be alone with him at three,

28:35.120 --> 28:37.560
when the race starts,
and I'll do the rest.

28:37.640 --> 28:38.960
Yeah?

28:39.040 --> 28:41.400
- Got a piece of chalk?
- Chalk?

28:41.480 --> 28:42.840
It's how the soldiers know...

28:42.920 --> 28:45.200
It doesn't matter, just give me
the fucking chalk.

28:55.760 --> 28:58.120
Lizzie, it's going to be all right, eh?

28:59.320 --> 29:00.960
I'll get to you, I promise.

29:01.040 --> 29:03.840
Before it can start,
I will be there.

29:12.880 --> 29:14.840
[people chattering]

29:17.600 --> 29:20.560
Keep them fucking guns ready.
Keep your guns ready.

29:20.640 --> 29:22.080
He's here, boss.

29:26.000 --> 29:27.800
[John] Coppers aren't moving.

29:28.440 --> 29:30.680
Stuck there like fucking gargoyles.

29:32.080 --> 29:34.560
Keep your wits about you, boys, all right?

30:09.880 --> 30:13.800
[announcer] Ladies and gentlemen,
the race will begin in four minutes.

30:13.880 --> 30:15.960
Please make your way...

30:36.640 --> 30:38.560
[Campbell]
Shouldn't you be busy?

30:40.840 --> 30:44.440
[Thomas] When you plan something well
there's no need to rush.

30:45.320 --> 30:49.600
Did you know something?
I actually trust you to do this.

30:53.840 --> 30:55.840
Do you think
there might be some

30:56.480 --> 30:59.600
measure of respect
developing between us?

30:59.680 --> 31:00.920
[announcer] Ladies and gentlemen,

31:01.000 --> 31:03.680
the runners and riders
are coming to order.

31:03.760 --> 31:05.120
Please take your seats.

31:05.200 --> 31:09.360
[Campbell] Old foes that have
grown to admire each other.

31:09.440 --> 31:12.440
And see each other's
professional virtues.

31:15.360 --> 31:16.680
Personally...

31:17.960 --> 31:18.960
...I think not.

31:19.040 --> 31:20.280
Oh, I think not.

31:23.200 --> 31:25.040
Well, I'd drink to that.

31:26.360 --> 31:29.240
[announcer] Ladies and gentlemen,
please be upstanding

31:29.320 --> 31:31.120
for the national anthem.

31:31.200 --> 31:33.840
[cheering and applauding]

31:36.160 --> 31:39.080
So, is the plan that
you'll stay together forever?

31:39.200 --> 31:40.720
[national anthem playing]

31:40.800 --> 31:45.320
Or, perhaps, she'll whore for you
and take her husband's money.

31:45.400 --> 31:46.800
Is that the plan?

31:48.480 --> 31:50.440
How wrong I was about her.

31:52.280 --> 31:54.320
[Thomas] I was wrong about her as well.

31:59.040 --> 32:00.680
You once said to me,

32:02.360 --> 32:04.840
that men like us
can never be loved.

32:06.800 --> 32:08.520
She loves me.

32:09.400 --> 32:10.920
She told me.

32:12.520 --> 32:14.280
She loves me.

32:16.040 --> 32:17.960
And all you got was a bullet

32:18.760 --> 32:21.200
and a fucking wolf head cane.

32:22.120 --> 32:25.320
Well, bolly for you.

32:28.080 --> 32:29.840
This I know.

32:31.400 --> 32:34.040
Ahead of you is damnation.

32:34.120 --> 32:36.720
But I have the love of God

32:37.360 --> 32:39.600
and the certainty of salvation.

32:39.680 --> 32:43.320
- [national anthem ends]
- [people cheer]

32:52.920 --> 32:54.680
I know what you did to Polly.

32:57.880 --> 33:00.280
I know what happened
to my uncle in jail.

33:04.600 --> 33:07.840
Today, it'll be me dead.

33:08.520 --> 33:09.800
Or you.

33:09.880 --> 33:13.800
But whoever it is,
he'll wake up in hell tomorrow.

33:18.840 --> 33:23.640
[announcer] Ladies and gentlemen,
the runners and riders are...

33:23.720 --> 33:26.040
[people cheering loudly]

33:27.320 --> 33:28.760
And they're off!

33:28.840 --> 33:30.440
[crowd cheers louder]

33:36.520 --> 33:38.880
[indistinct commentary over PA]

33:50.160 --> 33:52.440
Come on, girl. Come on.

33:55.640 --> 33:57.640
[speaks foreign language]

33:59.280 --> 34:00.720
[commentary continues]

34:05.760 --> 34:07.520
Come on, Tommy.

34:10.560 --> 34:13.159
- [woman laughing]
- [commentary continues]

34:25.199 --> 34:27.760
What a pretty dress.

34:34.600 --> 34:35.960
Take it off.

34:36.040 --> 34:38.120
Should we take this off first,
shall we?

34:38.199 --> 34:41.440
Lift up your dress
and show me that you're clean.

34:41.719 --> 34:42.920
Oh.

34:44.280 --> 34:46.520
Do as you're told.

34:48.199 --> 34:51.159
We should take it slow.
We've got all the time.

34:52.199 --> 34:53.320
[Lizzie gasps]

34:58.720 --> 35:00.640
- This area's closed off.
- What?

35:00.720 --> 35:03.800
The king will be coming this way
after the race. This area is secure.

35:03.880 --> 35:07.400
- You'll have to go around.
- [Thomas sighs]

35:08.360 --> 35:10.160
[cheering continues]

35:15.520 --> 35:17.280
[Lizzie yelps in pain]

35:19.560 --> 35:21.240
- Get the fuck off!
- [grunting]

35:21.920 --> 35:24.760
Fuck off!
Get the fuck off me!

35:33.440 --> 35:34.720
Oh, God!

35:37.200 --> 35:38.360
Hey.

35:38.440 --> 35:39.600
[grunts]

35:41.800 --> 35:43.120
[Lizzie grunting]

35:46.560 --> 35:48.040
Russell! [cocks gun]

35:48.120 --> 35:49.120
Fuck!

35:53.000 --> 35:54.560
[both yell]

36:07.800 --> 36:08.960
[Lizzie] Tommy!

36:09.040 --> 36:13.960
[announcer continues indistinct]

36:14.040 --> 36:15.240
[Lizzie] Tommy!

36:17.480 --> 36:18.720
[cocks gun]

36:20.480 --> 36:21.560
[Thomas screaming]

36:27.480 --> 36:28.960
[gun fires]

36:29.040 --> 36:31.240
- [panting]
- [crowd cheering loudly]

36:35.720 --> 36:38.320
Where were you!?
Where the fuck were you?

36:38.400 --> 36:39.960
Give me the gun, Lizzie.

36:40.840 --> 36:42.560
Lizzie.

36:42.640 --> 36:44.800
- I'm sorry.
- Fuck off. Fuck off!

36:45.440 --> 36:46.560
Just go.

36:47.000 --> 36:48.440
Go on. Go!

36:50.240 --> 36:52.360
[fires three shots]

37:01.120 --> 37:04.240
Officers, officers. I was taking a shit,

37:04.320 --> 37:07.360
and I heard voices, Irish voices,
and I heard a shot.

37:07.440 --> 37:09.920
I swear to God, there's a soldier
lying dead in there.

37:10.040 --> 37:11.480
This way.

37:13.720 --> 37:16.120
Get every man in uniform
around the king.

37:16.200 --> 37:18.640
Every man in uniform
around the king.

37:18.800 --> 37:20.160
Right now!

37:20.960 --> 37:22.800
The IRA are on the course.

37:22.880 --> 37:25.720
[man] Everyone to the king.
The Royal Enclosure now!

37:28.760 --> 37:31.440
All right, make ready boys,
this is it.

37:31.520 --> 37:34.760
You four get round the back.
Take three of your boys...

37:34.840 --> 37:36.760
[speaking indistinct]

37:36.840 --> 37:39.120
You stay with us.
But you stay back.

37:39.200 --> 37:40.200
[John] Let's go!

37:43.600 --> 37:45.120
Put your hands in the air.

37:48.040 --> 37:49.280
Turn around!

37:55.720 --> 37:56.960
Is there a problem?

37:57.040 --> 37:58.440
There are Fenians on the course.

37:58.520 --> 38:01.560
A soldier's been shot. Someone said
there was an Irishman in here.

38:02.280 --> 38:03.840
That is correct.

38:08.840 --> 38:10.000
Very sorry, sir.

38:11.760 --> 38:13.800
Chief of Security to His Majesty.

38:15.120 --> 38:17.560
I will now take command
of this situation.

38:54.200 --> 38:55.440
[door opens]

38:56.720 --> 38:57.800
[clears throat]

38:57.920 --> 38:59.760
[jazz music playing]

38:59.840 --> 39:03.000
Mr. Sabini, you're late. Have a seat.

39:09.840 --> 39:11.200
What happened to your nose?

39:11.280 --> 39:13.200
You wanna have that
brother of yours put down?

39:13.280 --> 39:15.040
Oh, I tried that. He bit the vet.

39:15.120 --> 39:20.080
I told the coppers that you're a fucking
gypsy racketeer Peaky Blinder.

39:20.800 --> 39:22.880
They're coming,
they're going to throw you out.

39:22.960 --> 39:24.600
Before the king comes up here.

39:24.680 --> 39:29.200
Well, from what I saw,
the police are a bit busy right now.

39:30.080 --> 39:32.200
Did you win any money today, Mr. Sabini?

39:36.200 --> 39:37.680
Where are our coppers?

39:38.680 --> 39:41.680
I said to that sergeant,
"one minute," he said two.

39:41.760 --> 39:42.960
He's fucking dead.

39:43.040 --> 39:45.320
Like I told you,
they're a bit busy.

39:45.920 --> 39:48.360
- Same as my boys.
- What the fuck does that mean?

39:48.440 --> 39:52.000
What does that mean?
Well, my boys are on the track.

39:52.080 --> 39:54.320
They're having a little bonfire.

39:54.640 --> 39:56.920
Gaming licenses, you know.

39:58.240 --> 39:59.280
[chuckles]

40:01.280 --> 40:02.280
Fuck.

40:05.640 --> 40:11.240
You place too much reliance on the police
for your security, Mr. Sabini.

40:11.320 --> 40:12.440
That was a mistake.

40:14.680 --> 40:16.560
No, no, think about who you are.

40:16.640 --> 40:18.320
Think about where you are.

40:18.760 --> 40:21.480
You pull a weapon,
you are the king's assassin.

40:21.560 --> 40:23.920
Now, sit down. Stay calm.

40:28.760 --> 40:29.760
Good.

40:31.360 --> 40:36.480
Now, your next mistake, Mr. Sabini,
was breaking your promise

40:36.560 --> 40:38.160
with Alfie Solomons.

40:39.120 --> 40:40.440
Hmm?

40:40.520 --> 40:45.280
You promised Alfie, and his bookies,
could come to Epsom.

40:45.360 --> 40:47.680
He was very hurt
when you said no.

40:48.640 --> 40:49.800
He was very hurt.

40:51.280 --> 40:53.880
That's why me and Alfie
are back in business.

41:05.400 --> 41:06.920
- [glass shatters]
- [women shriek]

41:09.520 --> 41:11.520
Hold it! Hold it!

41:11.600 --> 41:13.840
[Thomas] It's all right!
It's all right, officers,

41:13.920 --> 41:15.880
he's just a bad loser.

41:18.440 --> 41:22.360
[screaming] You fucking lose,
you fucking gypsy bastard!

41:22.440 --> 41:23.800
You lose!

41:28.720 --> 41:30.920
What the fuck are you looking at?

41:31.080 --> 41:33.720
[man] Step back! Move!

41:33.800 --> 41:36.360
You're now a prisoner
of the Red Right Hand.

41:42.120 --> 41:44.520
Now, take his hat and gun.

41:46.120 --> 41:47.240
Get him up.

41:48.400 --> 41:49.480
Easy.

41:52.280 --> 41:53.480
Take a seat.

41:54.840 --> 41:55.920
Sit down!

41:56.960 --> 41:58.040
[sighs]

42:01.640 --> 42:02.880
That's it.

42:04.320 --> 42:06.880
You make yourself
nice and comfortable.

42:08.360 --> 42:10.720
Just going for a wee drive,
Mr. Shelby.

42:14.080 --> 42:15.120
Let's go.

42:24.120 --> 42:26.960
[people chattering and laughing]

42:50.160 --> 42:52.440
I guessed and then John confirmed it.

42:53.880 --> 42:55.160
Guessed what?

42:55.960 --> 42:57.040
Who're you?

42:57.600 --> 42:59.160
I'm May Carleton.

42:59.720 --> 43:01.600
I trained Tommy Shelby's horse.

43:03.000 --> 43:06.280
And you're the woman who he said
was going to sail away.

43:09.680 --> 43:11.840
I see he didn't tell you about me.

43:13.960 --> 43:16.920
He did tell me about you.
I wonder if that's significant.

43:17.840 --> 43:19.240
Tell me what about you?

43:19.320 --> 43:21.040
You have any idea
where he is?

43:23.600 --> 43:25.200
I'm waiting for him here.

43:33.560 --> 43:35.240
There's been trouble
on the track.

43:36.160 --> 43:38.000
All the bookies have had
their licenses burnt.

43:38.080 --> 43:39.760
Shouldn't you be down with the horses?

43:39.840 --> 43:42.640
Which means they'll have to re-apply
for their legal pitches.

43:43.040 --> 43:45.680
It's all part of Tommy's plan
for the future.

43:45.760 --> 43:47.600
What do you know
about Tommy's future?

43:47.680 --> 43:49.600
The applications will be denied,
of course.

43:49.680 --> 43:53.160
And all the pitchers will be allocated
instead to Tommy's bookies.

43:56.400 --> 43:58.200
I know because I'll make sure of it.

44:00.120 --> 44:02.040
I have influence with the board.

44:05.440 --> 44:08.120
There's business and there's love.

44:08.200 --> 44:09.360
Is there?

44:11.280 --> 44:13.280
With Thomas Shelby?

44:16.280 --> 44:19.400
- What do you want from him?
- Same as you.

44:21.840 --> 44:23.440
I want to feel alive.

44:34.080 --> 44:35.920
Did he tell you my name?

44:41.760 --> 44:43.200
My name is Grace.

44:50.880 --> 44:53.640
[Campbell] In your statement
to the House, sir,

44:53.720 --> 44:56.080
I believe that you should say
that witnesses

44:56.160 --> 45:00.480
heard the killers say that
they were members of the IRA

45:00.560 --> 45:03.000
and that the killing
was in retribution

45:03.080 --> 45:06.640
for actions of the field marshal
in County Cork.

45:09.440 --> 45:11.320
Oh, our friend from Birmingham?

45:11.400 --> 45:12.520
[chuckles]

45:12.760 --> 45:14.280
He's being taken care of.

45:15.480 --> 45:16.520
Oh.

45:17.600 --> 45:19.080
A very good day, sir.

45:19.160 --> 45:21.400
- [footsteps approaching]
- I...

45:23.320 --> 45:25.320
Sorry, I... I must go.

45:26.080 --> 45:27.800
- Goodbye.
- [hangs up phone]

45:30.280 --> 45:31.760
Polly.

45:36.440 --> 45:38.320
Tommy told me you'd be here.

45:41.240 --> 45:42.200
Well...

45:42.880 --> 45:45.560
Then I told Tommy
it should be me who finishes you.

45:45.640 --> 45:46.720
[gun cocks]

45:50.200 --> 45:51.520
Small and weak.

45:52.440 --> 45:54.360
That's how you like it, isn't it?

45:55.400 --> 45:58.040
But this time,
small and weak has got a gun.

46:00.200 --> 46:02.400
Yeah, you wouldn't do that here.

46:02.880 --> 46:03.960
No?

46:05.360 --> 46:06.880
Do you see any coppers?

46:08.120 --> 46:09.480
Well, I don't.

46:09.920 --> 46:12.160
They're all around your precious king.

46:15.120 --> 46:16.200
[grunts]

46:22.600 --> 46:24.040
[grunts in pain]

46:28.040 --> 46:29.000
Polly.

46:29.440 --> 46:30.440
Polly.

46:33.000 --> 46:35.400
- Some part of you--
- I have no parts.

46:35.480 --> 46:38.160
Some part of you
wanted me as well.

46:38.240 --> 46:39.960
I know that. I felt it.

46:41.640 --> 46:46.000
And sure as hell some part of me
wants you still.

46:46.920 --> 46:49.480
And I'm just that part that...

46:50.880 --> 46:53.120
Some part of my soul.

46:53.960 --> 46:55.920
Some part of my soul.

46:56.720 --> 47:00.280
Curious how that is to me
and curious that it should be you.

47:01.720 --> 47:03.400
Opposites, perhaps.

47:04.320 --> 47:05.560
Opposites.

47:05.880 --> 47:07.160
And that...

47:09.560 --> 47:13.640
That thing sticking at my heart,
you own...

47:13.720 --> 47:15.320
You own part of that heart.

47:15.400 --> 47:18.040
You did. You did, Polly.

47:18.400 --> 47:19.680
You do.

47:20.160 --> 47:21.520
[gunshot]

47:22.160 --> 47:24.120
[staggered breathing]

47:31.040 --> 47:34.040
Don't fuck with the Peaky Blinders.

48:20.920 --> 48:23.000
[indistinct announcement over PA]

48:33.800 --> 48:36.360
Let's get you home.
Come on.

48:40.440 --> 48:42.880
[Arthur]
Look at this place, we own it!

48:43.960 --> 48:46.400
Put your money away
before I take it off you!

48:46.480 --> 48:48.400
- Fucking clean up!
- Get up!

48:49.880 --> 48:52.680
Lizzie, what the fuck
are you doing here?

48:52.760 --> 48:54.560
Working for Tommy,
the same as always.

48:54.640 --> 48:58.000
- You work for the Blinders.
- Hey, what happened to you?

48:58.080 --> 48:58.920
Fell over.

48:59.000 --> 49:00.760
Don't fucking give me that.

49:01.200 --> 49:02.400
Lizzie.

49:03.200 --> 49:05.680
Come here, come here,
come here, come here.

49:05.760 --> 49:07.720
Eh? Were you working?

49:08.640 --> 49:09.880
Yeah.

49:10.680 --> 49:13.880
Thought you'll earn yourself
a few bob at the races, eh?

49:13.960 --> 49:15.560
It's gotta stop, Lizzie.

49:15.640 --> 49:18.240
It's gotta stop.
Tommy's already told you.

49:18.800 --> 49:21.800
The toffs at the races are the worst.
You know that.

49:22.720 --> 49:25.280
Hey, come here, come here.
Look at me.

49:25.360 --> 49:26.560
Cheer up.

49:26.800 --> 49:28.040
We won.

49:28.800 --> 49:30.440
We fucking took Epsom.

49:30.520 --> 49:32.800
We kicked the Cockneys' fucking asses.

49:33.080 --> 49:34.560
Congratu-fucking-lations.

49:34.640 --> 49:36.560
[Arthur]
We fucking beat them, all right.

49:36.640 --> 49:40.480
John didn't even shoot his gun.
We're kings.

49:40.560 --> 49:42.840
Kings of the fucking world!

49:44.160 --> 49:48.800
John, I don't see the same thing
in your eyes that I see in Tommy's.

49:50.680 --> 49:51.960
You should get out.

49:53.480 --> 49:54.880
You should get out.

49:59.960 --> 50:01.480
Where is Tommy anyway?

50:01.880 --> 50:03.640
- [rattling]
- [engine rumbling]

50:16.120 --> 50:18.520
[brakes screech]

50:20.480 --> 50:21.800
[engine stops]

50:24.720 --> 50:26.120
[footsteps approaching]

50:30.080 --> 50:32.480
[wind whistling]

51:08.680 --> 51:11.080
[Thomas] Were any of you boys in France?

51:17.440 --> 51:19.680
Will you allow a man a cigarette?

51:22.920 --> 51:24.240
The Somme.

51:25.760 --> 51:27.040
Blackwoods.

51:31.800 --> 51:33.320
Somme, the bulge.

51:35.600 --> 51:36.720
Smoke.

51:58.160 --> 51:59.600
So fucking close.

52:06.680 --> 52:08.320
So fucking close.

52:19.120 --> 52:21.360
Oh, and there's a woman.

52:24.200 --> 52:25.560
Yeah.

52:26.480 --> 52:27.760
A woman...

52:29.800 --> 52:31.160
...I love.

52:33.400 --> 52:34.960
And I got close.

52:41.280 --> 52:44.640
Nearly got...
[shouting] fucking everything!

52:49.160 --> 52:50.640
[cocks gun]

53:10.480 --> 53:12.080
Oh, what the fuck.

53:14.480 --> 53:15.800
Get it done, boys.

53:26.920 --> 53:30.600
Comrade...
we have our orders.

53:31.760 --> 53:33.080
You know how it is.

53:38.120 --> 53:39.560
I know how it is.

53:54.040 --> 53:55.520
In the bleak mid-winter...

54:01.040 --> 54:03.840
At some point in the near future,
Mr. Churchill will want to

54:03.920 --> 54:06.440
speak to you in person, Mr. Shelby.

54:07.200 --> 54:09.160
[panting]

54:09.240 --> 54:10.720
He has a job for you.

54:11.880 --> 54:13.360
We will be in touch.

54:15.640 --> 54:17.440
Get out of the grave, tinker!

54:19.880 --> 54:21.960
Be on your fucking way!

54:23.720 --> 54:27.320
[song playing]

54:53.000 --> 54:54.200
[shouting] Fuck!

55:00.480 --> 55:03.200
[sobbing]

55:03.280 --> 55:04.520
[groans]

55:28.080 --> 55:29.680
[people chattering loudly]

55:34.760 --> 55:36.120
Well, all right!

55:38.160 --> 55:42.880
Ladies and gentlemen,
I'd like to raise a toast!

55:42.960 --> 55:44.600
[cheering]

55:44.680 --> 55:47.040
To the Small Heath Rifles.

55:47.120 --> 55:48.600
Small Heath Rifles!

55:48.680 --> 55:50.320
To the Lee boys...

55:50.400 --> 55:51.640
Yeah!

55:51.720 --> 55:54.240
And to the Peaky fucking Blinders.

55:54.320 --> 55:56.320
[cheering]

56:01.280 --> 56:03.440
Who's gonna stop us, eh?

56:07.120 --> 56:08.880
[all] Nobody!

56:17.280 --> 56:18.520
Nobody.

56:40.000 --> 56:41.200
[Thomas kicks table]

56:42.480 --> 56:44.160
Polly and I had a bet.

56:44.240 --> 56:45.560
[groans sleepily]

56:48.640 --> 56:50.080
One of us bet,

56:51.040 --> 56:52.920
you'd take the money and go.

56:55.320 --> 56:57.560
And one of us bet
you'd still be here.

56:59.600 --> 57:01.360
She wants me to stay.

57:04.040 --> 57:06.400
Mm. You know something, Michael?

57:09.120 --> 57:10.800
What Polly wants...

57:12.720 --> 57:15.920
...will always be a mystery to me.

57:26.880 --> 57:28.400
I've decided.

57:29.720 --> 57:31.360
I want to make real money.

57:33.280 --> 57:34.480
With you.

58:00.640 --> 58:02.560
I've got some ideas, Michael...

58:04.360 --> 58:06.360
...for the future of the company.

58:08.680 --> 58:10.080
And also,

58:13.000 --> 58:14.880
I'm planning on getting married.

58:14.960 --> 58:17.360
[theme song playing]
